menu "Apple T8140 (J700) platform power and fabric"
	depends on ARCH_APPLE || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on ARM64

config APPLE_T8140_MCC
	tristate "Apple T8140 system-level cache allocation owner"
	default y if ARCH_APPLE
	help
	  Enable system-level-cache allocation at boot on J700 (T8140), as the
	  native AppleT8140MCC driver does (mccEnableCacheMode step 3: AMCC
	  +0x82c = 0 on every plane, only when every plane already reports its
	  ways enabled and powered). Resume re-applies it and reboot, poweroff
	  and kexec run the native quiesce cache flush. On other machines the
	  driver does nothing.

	  Measured on J700: CPU memory latency ~100 -> 30 ns, and GPU depth-1
	  and depth-2 throughput +19-33%. Opt out with neo_mcc.enable=0.

endmenu
